Opportunity Radar migrations
============================

Alembic reads DATABASE_URL through app.core.config.load_settings(). The URL is
not stored in alembic.ini. ENABLE_INTERNAL_SCHEDULER must also contain a valid
typed-settings value; use false for migration commands.

Use only an explicit disposable database during migration development. For
example, in PowerShell:

    $env:DATABASE_URL = "sqlite+pysqlite:///C:/temp/radar-migration-test.db"
    $env:ENABLE_INTERNAL_SCHEDULER = "false"
    .\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic upgrade head
    .\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic current
    .\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic downgrade base

Do not omit DATABASE_URL when running Alembic: the application default points
to the real local opportunities.db file. Never stamp or migrate production
until an approved schema-only snapshot has been reviewed and reconciled with
this fresh-database baseline.

migrations/env.py imports app.models, app.lead_models, and
app.proposal_models so Base.metadata contains opportunities, sources, leads,
and proposals. It deliberately does not import app.main, start FastAPI, run a
scheduler, or execute scanners.

The initial baseline is validated only for a fresh database. The existing
Base.metadata.create_all() calls, SQLite runtime schema repair, manual
migration scripts, and scheduler-state table creation remain active for now.
They must be removed or replaced only after deployed-schema review.
